   "job_title": "Data Analyst Intern at Tech Mahindra",
   "description": "Tech Mahindra is hiring a Data Analyst Intern in Hyderabad for a 3-month, fully mentored internship. This is real, reviewed work on live projects — not a training sandbox or a certificate mill.\n\nAbout the internship\nYou will join the analytics team and work alongside people who do this professionally every day. From week one you own a scoped piece of work, take it through review, and see it ship.\n\nDay-to-day responsibilities\n• Write SQL queries to answer business questions.\n• Build and maintain dashboards stakeholders rely on.\n• Clean and reconcile data from multiple sources.\n• Present insights and recommendations to the team.\n• Document your work clearly so the next person can pick it up.\n• Take part in stand-ups, planning and review sessions with the team.\n\nTools and technologies you will use\nSQL, Advanced Excel, Power BI, Tableau, Python, Data Visualization, Dashboards, Statistics, Reporting, Data Cleaning — plus the internal tooling Tech Mahindra uses day to day.\n\nWhat you will learn\nHow analysis turns into decisions: framing the question, trusting the data, and communicating what it means.\n\nTeam structure\nYou report to a senior team member who acts as your mentor, inside a pod of 6-10 people. Weekly 1:1s track progress and a mid-internship review tells you exactly where you stand.\n\nWhat we expect from you\nCuriosity, ownership and clear communication. You are not expected to know every tool listed — you are expected to have solid fundamentals, ask good questions, and document what you do.\n\nDetails: ₹22,000/month stipend · 3 months · Work From Office · 2 openings · Hyderabad.\n\nIf you want to start a career in data analytics in Hyderabad, apply now. Responsibilities: Write SQL queries to answer business questions.; Build and maintain dashboards stakeholders rely on.; Clean and reconcile data from multiple sources.; Present insights and recommendations to the team.; Document your work so the next person can pick it up. Requirements: Education: pursuing or completed any Bachelor's or Master's degree; Graduation year: 2025, 2026 or 2027 batch; Minimum 60% / 6.0 CGPA (relaxable for candidates with strong practical projects); Technical skills: working knowledge of SQL, Advanced Excel, Power BI, Tableau; Soft skills: clear written communication, ownership, willingness to document work; Experience: none required — freshers welcome; prior projects or certifications are a plus.",
